Changes from the originals: the captures were renamed into our own `jev` query group so
the plugin does not depend on that repository, and the ecma file was copied into each of
javascript, typescript and tsx instead of using `; inherits:`.

Then, so that a unit is a function something binds a name to rather than any function
node:

  - ecma: bare (arrow_function) and bare (function_expression) are both narrowed to a
    variable_declarator, a pair, or a class field. Two patterns were added for a function
    one level deeper than its name, `const C = React.forwardRef(() => {...})` and the
    `const x = (() => {...})()` idiom, both restricted to a block body so that
    `useThing(s => s.value)` selectors are not units.
  - lua: bare (function_definition) is narrowed the same way, to an assignment, a local
    declaration or a table field.
  - go: func_literal is dropped, except one bound by a var declaration.
  - rust: function_signature_item is dropped, since a trait signature has no body.
